Sonrisa Watts is a behavioral researcher and artificial intelligence strategist from St. Kitts and Nevis. At age 24, Watts founded Emotion Encoded, an independent research initiative investigating cognitive-emotional barriers to AI adoption in high-stakes industries. By age 25, following her extensive mixed-methods studies and professional interviews with Caribbean medical specialists, her proprietary regional datasets captured global attention. This work culminated in a formal invitation from the Stanford University School of Medicine to integrate her findings into their Global AI Implementation Curriculum and first-author a landmark clinical AI implementation manuscript.
